{
  "id": "murphy-shakti-fibonacci-hippocampus",
  "name": "Shakti: Fibonacci and hippocampus, 4 phases (about 20 min)",
  "category": "signals",
  "evidence": "claim",
  "fidelity": "approximation",
  "dose": {"value": [10, 20], "unit": "mG", "plane": "unstated", "cite": "Murphy, Shakti demo"},
  "origin": "Todd Murphy, 8 Coil Shakti software (the vendor says the design was 'used in the lab in unpublished studies')",
  "uT": 1,
  "summary": "Murphy's four-phase Shakti session over both temporal lobes: a Fibonacci signal (4 min) and the hippocampal signal (5.25 min) take turns twice. The vendor calls it 'less well-tested' and publishes neither waveform. Both are rebuilt here; the vendor describes the Fibonacci signal in one sentence, so most of its build is this project's choice.",
  "setting": "Dark, quiet room, eyes closed; relax without meditating or falling asleep. The vendor says to start with the coils over the temporal lobes.",
  "schedule": "Vendor rules: at most once a week or every 72 h, never on consecutive days; a series of up to 6 sessions, then a 21-day break.",
  "notes": "The vendor's page gives the phases: Fibonacci 4 min, hippocampus 5.25 min, then both again (18.5 min of signal; the vendor calls it a 20-min session). On placement it says only 'you should start off using it over the temporal lobes'. Of the Fibonacci signal it says only that 'the magnetic field goes up and down in strength' at each Fibonacci node or harmonic (fibb_hipp_bat_consent.htm, 'Hippocampal and Fibonacci Signals'). This program plays all 8 coils together, four per side (front FT7/FT8, top C5/C6, back TP7/TP8, bottom T9/T10). The sites, the use of all 8 coils at once and the missing channel alternation are this project's choices. The Fibonacci table is rebuilt from that one sentence: bursts of 4 pulses at 100 Hz, 5 bursts a second, strengths rising 1, 1, 2, 3, 5, 8, 13, 21 and falling back over 3 s, repeated without a pause, on 0.5-ms points. The pulse timing, the 3-s rise and fall and the missing pause have no source. The hippocampal stand-in is the primed burst: one pulse, then four pulses 170 ms later, three times in 0.74 s (after Tsang 2004 p.5 [1017]), then 4 s of silence. Both are rebuilt from descriptions: the vendor's files are not published. Field strength: the vendor gives 10 to 20 mG without saying where it is measured (mono_proposal.htm, 'Formal Discussion'). This program's setting is the peak field 20 mm in front of each coil. At 1 uT there, the field is about 24 uT at the scalp. The support is the vendor's word; it calls the session 'less well-tested'. Independent sham-controlled tests of God-Helmet-type fields found no field effect (Granqvist 2005, double-blind; Gendle & McGrath 2012, where the experimenter knew the condition). The vendor reports headache or pressure in about 2% of users with hippocampal signals; if so, lower the intensity by one third. Not for people with epilepsy or a seizure history; stop at once on fear or any distress.",
  "targets": ["left-hippocampus-head", "left-hippocampus-body", "left-hippocampus-tail", "right-hippocampus-head", "right-hippocampus-body", "right-hippocampus-tail"],
